  "question": {
    "text": "The point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is translated parallel to the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> by <math><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math> units. If the new point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> lies in the third quadrant, then the equation of the line passing through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;and perpendicular to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> is"
  },
